NAME
       semodule - manage SELinux policy modules

SYNOPSIS
       semodule -l
       semodule -i MODULE.pp
       semodule -r MODULE

DESCRIPTION
       The SELinux policy is built from modules, one per service or area
       (apache, ssh, container...). semodule lists, installs and removes
       them. Custom modules are usually made by audit2allow -M from logged
       denials; on the RHCSA you fix labels, ports and booleans instead.

OPTIONS
       -l, --list-modules
              List the installed modules.

       -i, --install MODULE.pp
              Install a compiled module.

       -r, --remove MODULE
              Remove a module.

EXAMPLES
           semodule -l | grep apache

SEE ALSO
       audit2allow(1), semanage(8), sestatus(8)
